<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luigi Cadorna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1850">1850</a>–<a href="/years/1928">1928</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luigi Cadorna was chief of staff of the Italian army from 1914 to 1917. He launched eleven costly offensives on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soca">Isonzo</a> front and imposed harsh discipline, including summary executions. After the defeat at Caporetto in October–November 1917 he blamed his soldiers and was replaced by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armando-diaz">Armando Diaz</a>; he was nevertheless made a marshal of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 1924.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luigi-cadorna.jpg" alt="Luigi Cadorna" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Luigi_Cadorna_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
